  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1272",
      "html": "<p>Rineloricaria morrowi Fowler, 1940. Type locality: Contamana, Río Ucayali basin, Peru. Size: 16.5 cm SL. Temperature: 20–24°C.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1272",
      "html": "<p>South America: Ucayali River basin (Amazon, Upper Amazon, Marañón, Ucayali). IUCN Red List category: Least Concern (last assessed 2014).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1272",
      "html": "<p>The fish should be provided with half-pipe type refuges, which are often also used as spawning sites.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1272",
      "html": "<p>Adaptable omnivores, these fish will eat most foods, from cucumber or zucchini slices to frozen bloodworm or dry flake foods.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1272",
      "html": "<p>Peaceful and not territorial.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1272",
      "html": "<p>Males grow short spines on the top of their heads and on the pectoral fins.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1272",
      "html": "<p>Unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
